ready: 1
kind: rule
id: consolidation.rule.promotion-gates
display_id: RULE-CONSOLIDATION-GATES
module: consolidation
title: When a promotion applies and when it becomes a suggestion
summary: >-
  Decides whether a promotion may be proposed, must wait for review, or may apply automatically.
notes: >-
  Beliefs and values need enough evidence to be proposed at all, identity layers always wait for
  review, and other promotions apply automatically only when the caller asked for that and the
  trust gate allows it.
owner: crates/kernle-core/src/consolidation/gates.rs::check
inputs:
- name: proposal
  source: The proposed memory, its kind, confidence, and cited evidence
  source_kind: derived
- name: automatic promotion
  source: Whether the caller asked for automatic promotion; sleep always does
  source_kind: parameter
- name: gate decision
  source: The trust gate's decision
  source_kind: return
rules:
- trust.rule.input-gate
params:
- name: belief minimum evidence
  value: '3'
  unit: episodes or notes
- name: belief minimum confidence
  value: '0.6'
- name: value minimum evidence
  value: '5'
  unit: beliefs or episodes, at least one a protected belief
table:
  columns:
  - Situation
  - Outcome
  rows:
  - - A belief with fewer than the minimum evidence or below the minimum confidence
    - Not proposed; the source is marked skipped
  - - A value with fewer than the minimum evidence, or none of it protected beliefs
    - Not proposed; the source is marked skipped
  - - A value, a self-narrative, or a foundational belief
    - Suggestion held as an identity layer
  - - The trust gate holds or quarantines the change
    - Suggestion with the gate's reason
  - - Confidence below 0.5
    - Suggestion held for low confidence
  - - Automatic promotion asked for, and none of the above
    - Applied through the memory write
  - - Automatic promotion not asked for
    - Suggestion held because review was requested
precedence:
- Rows are checked top to bottom; the first match decides.
default: Suggestion held because review was requested
rationale: >-
  Identity layers should be hard to write and easy to read. A value or self-narrative shapes every later
  session, so automatic processing only ever proposes them; the agent's own deliberate call or the owner's
  review makes them real.
